        "text_preview": "Vide impugned order dated 14.12.2022, the learned Sessions Judge allowed the appeal and set aside the order of the trial Magistrate, presumably, on the ground that the relief relating to residence to an aggrieved person can be granted only "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "789d0ab3f08a45f19a664ade9d08901b_19",
        "summary_section": "issue",
        "labels": [
          "ISSUE"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:issue"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n10) The issue which is required to be determined in this petition is as to whether a Magistrate, while considering the grant of interim order in favour of an aggrieved person in terms of Section 23 of the DV Act, can pass an order of resid"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a823eae8e51e484a8003d481d141538d_20",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In order to determine this issue, the provisions contained in Section 23 of the DV Act are required to be noticed."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "97e3c277929a44239dda99a0a65d1a4a_21",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The same are reproduced as under:\n\"23. Power to grant interim and ex parte orders.--(1) In any proceeding before him under this Act, the Magistrate may pass such interim order as he deems just and proper."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "00dce762a55748008f1ae690ce1b81d4_22",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "(2) If the Magistrate is satisfied that an application prima facie discloses that the respondent is committing, or has committed an act of domestic violence or that there is a Page |4 likelihood that the respondent may commit an act of dome"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "10871f7a90c74e7b9f68f39c9e477959_23",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Section 18 of the DV Act relates to protection orders,\nSection 19 relates to residence orders, Section 20 relates to monetary reliefs, Section 21 relates to custody orders and Section 22 relates to compensation orders."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "607c86f9dc5046028a3ca3fa9ca22887_24",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Thus, it is clear that interim orders of the aforesaid nature, which includes an order relating to residence, can be passed by a Magistrate in exercise of his powers under Section 23 of the DV Act."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8c9aa4cc027a4b45a09fc5c5f881dc9c_25",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n12) The next question that is required to be determined is as to at what stage an interim order can be passed by a Magistrate in exercise of his powers under Section 23 of the DV Act."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ffadbfb128ad415bbd2d7dd0d8eb492d_26",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Since we are concerned with the residence orders in the present case, therefore, it would be apt to notice the provisions contained in Section 19 of the DV Act, which read as under:\n\"19. Residence orders.--(1) While disposing of an applicat"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "31a9a68fd9ec4fddab008873cdc3987e_27",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Provided that no order under clause (b) shall be passed against any person who is a woman."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "997a940c94a04a6aa016c09898ed8602_28",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n(2) The Magistrate may impose any additional conditions or pass any other direction which he may deem reasonably necessary to protect or to provide for the safety of the aggrieved person or any child of such aggrieved person."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "95e8f69f3ed2469fb6028f8f8115b2ea_29",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n(3) The Magistrate may require from the respondent to execute a bond, with or without sureties, for preventing the commission of domestic violence."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c6639a96dd95473d872bd48a64ea0b6f_30",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n(4) An order under sub-section (3) shall be deemed to be an order under Chapter VIII of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 (2 of 1974) and shall be dealt with accordingly."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "3541eb34eabc46c98f4964fabb2cbb94_31",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n(5) While passing an order under sub-section (1), sub- section (2) or sub-section (3), the court may also pass an order directing the officer in charge of the nearest police station to give protection to the aggrieved person or to assist h"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "749d63e8d19b4b68ab5fc45438a3708e_32",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n13) A perusal of the aforesaid provision reveals that residence orders can be passed by a Magistrate while disposing of main application under Section 12 of the DV Act, meaning thereby that a residence order can be passed by a Magistrate a"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "26ac7092eef148c6b59e367ccf656ec8_33",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "However, when we read the provisions of Section 19 in conjunction with Section 23 of the DV Act, it becomes clear that while final residence order can be passed by a Magistrate at the time of final disposal of the petition under Section 12 "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "370320eb5fbb483ab5aeb8a155909935_34",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n14) Section 23 of the DV Act gives power to a Magistrate to pass an interim order of the nature as provided in the said provision."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "726b2f164d17469dbbdab5ae17821ccd_35",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Residence order is an urgent relief to protect a woman from her Mst Shameema Begum vs Javid Iqbal Khan on 21 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/129556029/\n4 taking shelter on road.\nPage |7"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "28899c930a06498eb72cb21fc677a39d_36",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, passing of an interim order of the nature as defined under Section 19 of the Act is well within the jurisdiction of a Magistrate."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "9f7f6f1b66df49aa822fe145ddfda4b7_37",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n15) The view taken by the learned Appellate Court is clearly contrary to the provisions contained in Section 23 of the DV Act and the object of the said Act which is to provide immediate relief to an aggrieved person from domestic violence"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "08190d4d68714dad8bafe6ae7090dbb9_38",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Thus, the impugned order passed by the learned Sessions Judge is not sustainable in law."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8ec144f9a8bd447d870b84461f64602a_39",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The same has resulted in grave injustice to the petitioner who has been deprived of a shared household because of the impugned order."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "fc564fb63445450cb807e75d37064836_40",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS",
          "explicit_leakage_phrase"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [
          {
